From 5473b04edf9735a0fe11401b6ea1528aa0cb979c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 00:36:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] v112-skeptic: bit-exact and no-louder guards for
 velocityDb; percentile edge tests; stale 1..3 comments; 2.0 notes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

dynamic-range.test.mjs compares velocityDb with a frozen copy of the 1.1.1 formula (=== over v step 0.001, ranges
1..3 step 0.01) and checks no v is louder past 3× than at 3×. touch-curve tests cover unsorted input, junk, equal
notes, a low and a high outlier, 10 notes. CONTRACT_CHANGES records that lane-touch's D43 law differs past 3× and
that 2.0's store keeps an imported value above 3 as 3; the release note says the same in plain words.

